    "narrative": "Our lineup anchor today is undoubtedly **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who commands a 76.94 efficiency score. He draws a highly favorable matchup against Montero, whose 4.43 xERA provides the perfect runway for a high-ceiling performance. We are also projecting significant upside from **Cal Raleigh** (64.16), who benefits from a favorable park factor and a solid platoon advantage against Fried. While **Gleyber Torres** is batting leadoff against a southpaw, his 59.17 score is bolstered by a strong 13% platoon adjustment, making him a cornerstone of our middle infield production tonight.\n\nThe primary constraint on today\u2019s roster construction is the weather risk in the Tampa Bay matchup, which threatens our efficiency across **Bryce Harper**, **Luis Arraez**, and our primary speed threat, **Justin Crawford**. Despite the 44% rain risk, **Bryce Harper** remains a mandatory start due to his superior xwOBA metrics, though his floor is undeniably shaky if the game is shortened. **Justin Crawford** occupies a marginal scoring tier (51.25) largely due to his spot in the nine-hole; however, given our league\u2019s aggressive prioritization of SB, he remains rostered over potential alternatives to ensure we don't cede ground in our scarcest category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was navigating the utility spot against **JJ Bleday**. While **JJ Bleday** landed at a 45.40, he barely eclipsed the internal threshold required to keep him in the lineup, largely due to a harsh 14% penalty regarding his platoon matchup against Martin. With **Will Smith** and **Tyler Freeman** sidelined on the IL, and **Lawrence Butler** and **Daulton Varsho** absent from the schedule entirely, our bench depth is currently limited. We are monitoring the status of **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Zack Gelof**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Alex Freeland** for any late-breaking lineup changes, but for now, we are comfortable rolling with the current configuration despite the volatile weather outlook for our core bats.",
